    <string name="set_privacy">Privacy</string>
    <string name="set_privacy_body">No account, no analytics, no location, camera, microphone or contacts. Data stays on this phone. The network is used only for Wi-Fi remotes on your home network and code packs you download.</string>
    <string name="about_body">A universal infrared remote for phones with a built-in IR emitter. Codes are labelled by evidence level; compatibility is only claimed where evidence exists.</string>
    <string name="about_protocols">Supported protocols</string>
    <string name="about_limitations">Known limitations</string>
    <string name="about_limitations_body">• No IR learning: the phone has no IR receiver.\n• The real AC state cannot be read; the app shows the last requested state.\n• No protocol has been confirmed on hardware by this project yet; levels rise only when users confirm codes.\n• Electra 104-bit is marked Alpha upstream; its carrier frequency is a guess.\n• Broadlink captures do not record the carrier; 38 kHz is assumed.\n• Protocol details in diagnostics are shown in English.</string>
    <string name="about_notices">Open-source notices</string>
    <string name="about_use_esp">Electra 104-bit, Gree and Coolix encoders are ported from this library (LGPL-2.1); see NOTICE.md.</string>
    <string name="about_use_kelon">KELON168 byte tables, checksums and power sequences.</string>
    <string name="about_use_tadiran">Tadiran 64-bit encoder; shows Tadiran \'Sakal\' remotes use the Gree frame.</string>
    <string name="about_use_electra34">Electra 34-bit Manchester encoder (public domain).</string>
    <string name="about_use_central">Real captures of an Electra/Tadiran central unit used as reference vectors.</string>
    <string name="about_use_smartir">Bundled captured AC, TV and fan codes; reference captures for tests.</string>
    <string name="about_use_reference">Timing reference for consumer protocols.</string>
    <string name="about_use_flipper">File format supported by the importer; no files are bundled.</string>
    <string name="about_use_irdb">CSV format supported by the importer for files you provide; the database is not bundled or downloaded because its license requires notifying the project.</string>
    <string name="about_use_android">Application framework libraries.</string>
    <string name="about_report">Report a compatibility result</string>
    <string name="about_report_body">Use the code wizard\'s Yes/No answers: results are stored with your phone model in Verification history and can be exported from the Code database page.</string>
